# Cross-file monomorphization (extends the same-file `monomorphize_struct.br`):
# constructs `Wrapper<string>` via turbofish from a DIFFERENT file than the one
# declaring `Wrapper<T>` (monomorphize_cross_file_lib.br). The transpiler
# specializes a non-generic `Wrapper_string` clone into the DECLARING file's own
# emitted module (avoiding a duplicate definition if more than one file called the
# same instantiation), and rewrites this file's call site to a plain call on that
# specialized name — a bare identifier, since the generated Rust is one flat,
# concatenated namespace (see monomorphize.rs's module doc comment).
use monomorphize_cross_file_lib

let w = Wrapper<string>("hi")
print w.value
